## Findings
1. advisory — brief:44 [severity: S2] The terminal range `scrollWidth − offsetWidth` is not the CSSOM maximum of `scrollLeft` (`scrollWidth − clientWidth`). `.board__columns` keeps `scrollbar-gutter: stable` (w025.css:1163). Wherever that gutter is non-zero, the thumb's travel is out of step with the container by the gutter width: in ordinary Chromium (not `--hide-scrollbars`), on Windows or Linux classic scrollbars, the thumb reaches the track's right edge while gutter-width content is still unscrolled, and the cue stays hidden when the overflow is no wider than the gutter. The served row cannot see this. It runs only under `--hide-scrollbars`, where offsetWidth equals clientWidth. It also checks the offset only at the initial position and at a terminal it sets itself to `scrollWidth − offsetWidth` (cue-tests.patch, w406.spec.ts). So "proportional synchronized thumb" (brief:54) and "not counted twice" promise more than the row proves for the Patron's ordinary browser. Replacement for brief:44: "Thumb width is `trackWidth × clientWidth / scrollWidth`; thumb offset is `(trackWidth − thumbWidth) × scrollLeft / (scrollWidth − clientWidth)`, the container's own maximum `scrollLeft`, with finite zero-range guards and values clamped to the track. The served row sets its terminal offset to `scrollWidth − clientWidth`." The kill-78 regex and served row 78 change with it. An alternative fix keeps the formula and adds this limit to brief:54: "synchronization is proven only where the native gutter is zero (`--hide-scrollbars`, overlay scrollbars); with a non-zero gutter the thumb may reach its right bound up to one gutter width early." [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: none: a served row that launches with scrollbars shown and asserts thumb offset against `scrollLeft / (scrollWidth − clientWidth)` at a mid-range offset and at the true terminal

